docs {
  # Met Gallery: the Met Collection API, by hand

  Every request the app makes, plus the odd answers it has to cope with.
  Each request asserts what the app relies on, so running the collection
  is a quick check that the API still behaves the way the code assumes.

  Choose the **Met** environment first. Its `baseUrl` is the same address
  as `COLLECTION_BASE_URL` in the project's `.env`.

  Run everything from this folder:

  ```sh
  npx @usebruno/cli run --env Met
  ```

  Go easy on it. The firewall in front of the API allows roughly 80
  requests a minute per IP address (not the 80 a second the documentation
  mentions) and answers the rest with a 403. The whole collection is 14
  requests.

  API documentation: https://metmuseum.github.io/
}
